/*
 * The ORDER leg for the plain-`T*` parameter guard, and the reason that guard is
 * record-then-resolve rather than a call-site check. cflat emits IR as it walks, so a callee
 * defined BELOW its call site is still a bare declaration when the call is emitted: the
 * callee-side escape fact is not answerable yet, and ParameterProvablyRetainsArgument
 * correctly reports "no proof" (unknown accepts, by design). The call is therefore RECORDED
 * and re-asked at end of module, where every body is complete.
 *
 * The offending call is in an IMPORTED module (Test/library/temp_uniq_plain_param_mod.cb), not
 * here, which is the second half of what this leg covers: by the time the deferred pass runs,
 * the compiler's own sourceFileName is THIS file, so the record has to carry the file the call
 * was written in. Measured before that was fixed: the module's call at
 * `temp_uniq_plain_param_mod.cb(14,4)` was reported as a location in the IMPORTING file. Note
 * `expect_error` matches the message TEXT, never the `file(line,col):` prefix, so this leg pins
 * the deferred resolution and the cross-module reach; the file attribution itself is checked by
 * reading the diagnostic (scratch/rvw_mainimp.cb + scratch/rvwmod/ hold the reviewer's probe).
 *
 * This leg lives in its own file because the diagnostic is DEFERRED: a scoped
 * `expect_error(...) { }` block closes before end-of-module resolution runs and would print
 * "expected error ... did not occur", i.e. exactly the opposite of the truth. The bare
 * file-scope form is the one that stays armed to the end of the compile, and it covers the
 * rest of the scope - so one leg per file is a structural constraint here, not a style choice.
 * The immediate-path legs for the same guard live in err_unique_borrow_into_field.cb.
 *
 * Measured before the guard (-o + run): `v=99 same=1 dtors=1` - the temp's destructor freed
 * the pointee and the read aliased a freshly reallocated block. Mutation-tested: deleting
 * the ResolveTempUniqueFieldArgEscapes call at the end of the walk makes this file exit 1
 * with "expected error ... did not occur", while every leg in the sibling file still passes.
 */
expect_error("call to 'keepModGlobal': cannot pass unique field 'makeModBox.t' of a temporary to plain pointer parameter 'n' - 'keepModGlobal' stores that pointer into a global");

import "temp_uniq_plain_param_mod.cb";

extern int main()
{
    offendFromImportedModule();
    return 0;
}
